<section class="check-understanding"><title>Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="4da44566-324d-4927-8c3f-81dbeb4e1863" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here.</para><para> Identify the \(x\) coordinate of the solution. </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The answer is 1.</para><para>The answer is 1.</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="efc3fc12-dbd8-4bf8-9e76-6c35c06b71c5" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here.</para><para> Identify the \(y\) coordinate of the solution. </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The answer is 1.</para><para>The answer is 1.</para></solution></exercise></section>
<!--Q#4-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Find the sum or difference of the two original equations that would enable the system to be solved. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here are some samples.</para>
    <list>
      <item> Sample Answer 1: \(8y=16 \)</item>
      <item> Sample Answer 2: \(y=2 \)</item>
      <item> Sample Answer 3: \(8x−2y=4 \)</item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


