<!--Q#6-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Make an observation about the graph. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
    <para>All three lines intersect at \((1, 2)\). If students graph \(8y=16\), the graph of the new equation is a horizontal line. If students graph \(8x−2y=4\), the graph of the new equation is a new line between the two original lines.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

