<exercise data-wait-for-event="RFM1">
  <problem>
    <title>Extending Your Thinking</title>
    <para>Mai wonders what would happen if we multiply equations. That is, we multiply the expressions on the left side of the two equations and set them equal to the expressions on the right side of the two equations.</para>
    <para>Use System B to answer questions 1 – 4.</para>
    <para>System B</para>
    <para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{c}2x+y=4\\x-y=11\end{array}\right.\)</para>
    
    <para> Write out an equation that you would get if you multiply the two equations in this manner. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. \((2x+y)(x−y)=44\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--End interaction-->

